{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ew_interface_knot","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ew_interface_knot","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ew_interface_knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ew_interface_knot","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L49-L70","doc":"**Content statement** (from manuscript):\n\n**Definition (electroweak interface knot $\\Delta_I$).**\n*Let $R$ be the categorical coefficient ring with $q \\in R$\ngeneric (not a root of unity in $R$, $q \\neq 1$). Inside the\n$n = 6$ Hecke algebra $H_6(q)$ over $R$, the **electroweak\ninterface knot** $\\Delta_I$ is a non-empty word in the\n**adjacent-pair generators** $\\sigma_2$ and $\\sigma_4$ — i.e. the\ngenerators that connect the disjoint strand-pairs $(1,2),\n(3,4), (5,6)$ on which the EW carriers\n$W \\leftrightarrow \\sigma_1^{\\,4}$, $Z \\leftrightarrow \\sigma_3^{\\,6}$,\n$H \\leftrightarrow \\sigma_5^{\\,8}$ act\n([`conj:hoefsmit-ew-cell-content`](#conj:hoefsmit-ew-cell-content)).*\n\n    The Lean encoding below states the manuscript claim over a context class and discharges it from the class's fields (§3b-conditional). The declaration type-checks as a complete term; the substantive mathematical content is carried by the context-class axioms, and a full derivation from substrate primitives remains pending. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.claim_iii_bar_self_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.claim_iii_bar_self_duality","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (iii) — Bar-self-duality breakdown is\nstructural: the EW interface knot uses the 2 adjacent-pair\ngenerators `(σ_2, σ_4)` connecting the 3 disjoint strand pairs\nthat carry the EW exponents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.n_disjoint_strand_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.n_disjoint_strand_pairs","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Number of disjoint strand-pairs on which the EW carriers act\n(`(1,2), (3,4), (5,6)` for `H_6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.n_adjacent_pair_generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.n_adjacent_pair_generators","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L38-L38","doc":"Number of adjacent-pair generators used by the EW interface\nknot (`σ_2` and `σ_4` for `H_6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.claim_ii_ew_carrier_exponents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.claim_ii_ew_carrier_exponents","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (ii) — EW-carrier exponents:\n`(W, Z, H) ↔ (σ_1^4, σ_3^6, σ_5^8)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.claim_i_strand_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.claim_i_strand_count","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (i) — Strand-count identity: the EW\ninterface knot lives in `H_6(q)` (n_strands = 6). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.exp_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.exp_H","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.exp_Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.exp_Z","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.exp_W","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.exp_W","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L26-L26","doc":"EW-carrier exponents `(σ_1^4, σ_3^6, σ_5^8)` for `(W, Z, H)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.n_strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.n_strands","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L24-L24","doc":"Strand count of the EW interface knot (manuscript: `n = 6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.CategoricalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.CategoricalObj","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L22-L22","doc":"The categorical object / monoidal structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EwInterfaceKnotContext","kind":"class","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ew_interface_knot.lean#L18-L47","doc":"Abstract context for the `ew_interface_knot` claim — manuscript-themed\ntyped fields below; `holds` carries the residual `Prop` claim. ","signatureChunk":0}]}